    key_insight="The tightest constraint on the schedule always comes from the single most frequent task (or tasks, if there's a tie), since scheduling it optimally with the mandatory cooldown gaps determines a minimum schedule length; if there are enough other distinct tasks to fill every gap, the schedule can be fully packed with no idle time, in which case the answer is just simply the total number of tasks.",
