    edge_case="n=0, meaning no cooldown is needed at all. formula = (max_freq-1)*(0+1)+max_count = max_freq - 1 + max_count. Taking the max with len(tasks) will typically just resolve to len(tasks) directly, since with no cooldown restriction, tasks can just be run back-to-back in any order, needing exactly as many slots as there are tasks.",
    edge_case_say="Let me check n=0, meaning there's no cooldown restriction at all — the formula still computes correctly, but the max with len(tasks) naturally resolves to just the total number of tasks, since we can run everything back-to-back with no idle time needed.",
