        ("Me", "I'll count each task's frequency, find the maximum frequency, and how many tasks tie for it. The schedule structure is dominated by the most frequent task, which needs (max_freq - 1) complete cycles of (n+1) slots each, plus a final chunk holding however many tasks tied for that max frequency."),
        ("Me", "But if there are enough other distinct tasks to fill every gap, no idle time is actually needed, so I take the max of that formula and just the total number of tasks."),
        ("Me", "Let me code that — counting frequencies, then applying the formula."),
        ("Me", "Tracing tasks A,A,A,B,B,B with n=2: both A and B tie for max frequency 3, giving a formula result of 8, matching a valid schedule like A-B-idle-A-B-idle-A-B."),
        ("Me", "Edge case: n=0 means no cooldown at all, and the max with the total task count correctly resolves to just running everything back-to-back."),
        ("Me", "Final complexity: O(t) time to count frequencies, O(1) extra space."),
